<div class="card">
    <h2>Step 1: Privacy Notice</h2>
    <p class="form-hint">Please read the full notice below. The acknowledgment form is in Step 2.</p>

    <h3>Patient details</h3>
    <div class="form-row">
        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="patient_name">Patient Name</label>
            <input type="text" id="patient_name" name="patient.name"
                   value="{{ patient.name }}">
        </div>
        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="patient_birth_date">Date of Birth</label>
            <input type="date" id="patient_birth_date" name="patient.birth_date"
                   value="{{ patient.birthDate }}">
        </div>
        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="patient_united_kingdom_nhs_number">NHS Number</label>
            <input type="text" id="patient_united_kingdom_nhs_number" name="patient.united_kingdom_nhs_number"
                   value="{{ patient.unitedKingdomNhsNumber }}" placeholder="e.g. 943 476 5919">
        </div>
    </div>

    <h3>Practice configuration</h3>
    <p class="form-hint">Edit these fields to match your practice. They appear inside the notice text below.</p>
    <div class="form-row">
        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="practice_name">Practice Name</label>
            <input type="text" id="practice_name" name="practice_config.practice_name"
                   value="{{ practice_config.practiceName }}" placeholder="[Insert name of practice]">
        </div>
        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="data_protection_officer">Data Protection Officer</label>
            <input type="text" id="data_protection_officer" name="practice_config.data_protection_officer"
                   value="{{ practice_config.dataProtectionOfficer }}" placeholder="[Insert DPO name and contact details]">
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="form-row">
        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="research_organisations">Research Organisations</label>
            <input type="text" id="research_organisations" name="practice_config.research_organisations"
                   value="{{ practice_config.researchOrganisations }}">
        </div>
        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="audit_body">Audit Body</label>
            <input type="text" id="audit_body" name="practice_config.audit_body"
                   value="{{ practice_config.auditBody }}" placeholder="e.g. Healthcare Quality Improvements Partnership">
        </div>
        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="gdpr_basis">GDPR Article 9 Basis</label>
            <select id="gdpr_basis" name="practice_config.gdpr_basis">
                <option value="" {% if practice_config.gdprBasis == "" %}selected{% endif %}>&mdash;</option>
                <option value="consent" {% if practice_config.gdprBasis == "consent" %}selected{% endif %}>Consent &mdash; Article 9(2)(a)</option>
                <option value="research" {% if practice_config.gdprBasis == "research" %}selected{% endif %}>Research &mdash; Article 9(2)(j)</option>
            </select>
        </div>
    </div>

    <h3>Medical research and service planning</h3>
    <p>
        {{ practice_config.practiceName | default(value="[Insert name of practice]") }} uses and shares
        information from your medical records to support medical research and to help plan NHS services.
        Information is shared with {{ practice_config.researchOrganisations | default(value="[Insert research organisations]") }}
        and national NHS organisations, either with your explicit consent or where the law allows.
    </p>

    <h3>Checking quality of care &mdash; national clinical audits</h3>
    <p>
        {{ practice_config.practiceName | default(value="[Insert name of practice]") }} contributes to
        national clinical audits, which are used to check and improve the quality of care provided to
        patients across the NHS. Data is sent to {{ practice_config.auditBody | default(value="[Insert audit body]") }}
        for this purpose.
    </p>

    <h3>National screening programmes</h3>
    <p>
        The NHS provides national screening programmes so that certain diseases can be detected at an
        early stage. These include bowel cancer, breast cancer, cervical cancer, aortic aneurysms, and
        a diabetic eye screening service. The law allows us to share your contact information with
        the UK Health Security Agency so that you can be invited to the appropriate screening programmes.
    </p>

    <h3>Lawful basis under UK GDPR</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Article 6(1)(e)</strong> &mdash; processing necessary for a task carried out in the public interest.</li>
        {% if practice_config.gdprBasis == "research" %}
        <li><strong>Article 9(2)(j)</strong> &mdash; processing for scientific research purposes.</li>
        {% else %}
        <li><strong>Article 9(2)(a)</strong> &mdash; the data subject has given explicit consent.</li>
        {% endif %}
        <li><strong>Article 9(2)(h)</strong> &mdash; preventative medicine and the management of health-care systems.</li>
    </ul>
</div>
